<?xml version="1.0"?>
<!--
  ===========================================================================
  THE TRANSFER PAGE'S STYLES WERE WRITTEN BUT NEVER LOADED
  ===========================================================================
  components/_checkout.less has carried the whole `.spartrak-instapay__*` block
  since the page was built (Figma 586:7352 / 586:7420, with the 440 rules in the
  mobile section). It compiles into css/spartrak-checkout.css — which was
  enqueued on checkout_index_index and checkout_onepage_success and on nothing
  else, so this handle rendered the markup with no stylesheet behind it: an
  unstyled native file input, no dropzone, no brand ring.

  Only the page bundle was missing. spartrak-components.css and the foundations
  load globally, which is why the header and footer looked correct while
  everything between them did not.

  ===========================================================================
  IT SHARES THE CHECKOUT'S STYLESHEET RATHER THAN GETTING ITS OWN
  ===========================================================================
  The `.spartrak-instapay__*` rules are ~370 of the 3,270 lines in
  _checkout.less, about 750 bytes gzipped, and they match nothing outside this
  page — so splitting them into a fourth bundle looks like the tidier answer.
  It measures worse.

  This page is only ever reached by redirect from the checkout, immediately
  after place-order. spartrak-checkout.css is therefore already in cache,
  under the identical URL, every single time: sharing it costs ZERO requests
  and ZERO bytes here. A dedicated bundle would instead cost one cold request
  on a page the shopper hits mid-payment, on whatever connection they happen to
  be on, to save the checkout page 750 bytes it had already paid for.

  Fewer requests on the critical page wins (CLAUDE.md section 13). It is also
  the precedent already set one handle over: checkout_onepage_success.xml
  enqueues this same file for the same reason.

  If this page ever becomes reachable cold — a link in the confirmation SMS,
  say, or a "finish your payment" link from the account area — that premise
  breaks and the split becomes the right call.
-->
<page xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance"
      xsi:noNamespaceSchemaLocation="urn:magento:framework:View/Layout/etc/page_configuration.xsd">
    <head>
        <css src="css/spartrak-checkout.css"/>
    </head>
</page>
